IMPORT prelude

-- Competition Act 2004 (Singapore) -- who Part 3 reaches (s 33(4), (5)); the three prohibitions: anti-competitive agreements
-- (s 34 with the Third Schedule exclusions), abuse of a dominant position (s 47 with the Third Schedule) and mergers that
-- substantially lessen competition (s 54 with the Fourth Schedule); the cap on the Commission's financial penalty (s 69(3), (4));
-- whether an appeal suspends a decision (s 71(3)); the investigation offences (ss 75, 77) and the general penalty (s 83); and the
-- right of private action (s 86).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CA2004.txt. The deposit
-- labels itself as incorporating amendments up to and including 1 December 2021; later amendments are annotated in the body, the
-- latest seen being S 18/2026 (in force 19 January 2026, Fourth Schedule para 1(a)), with Act 13 of 2025 (in force 1 July 2025)
-- and Act 25 of 2021 (in force 1 April 2022) also shown.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 4 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the rules a business or its adviser
-- meets: whether conduct is caught, the exclusions, the penalty ceiling, the offences around investigations and private claims.
-- Not encoded: the Commission's constitution, finance and staff (Part 2), block exemptions (ss 36-41), notification for guidance or
-- decision (ss 42-53, 55A-60), commitments (ss 60A, 60B), investigation powers themselves (ss 61A-67), the Appeal Board (ss 72-74),
-- the content of s 69 directions other than the penalty cap, ss 76, 78-82, 84, 85, 87-104, and the First and Second Schedules.
-- Ministerial orders under the Third Schedule (paras 3, 4, 8) and s 33(5) are taken as given facts; none was retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Competition Act 2004 -- prohibitions`

§§ `33(4), (5) -- who Part 3 reaches`

-- s 33(1): Part 3 applies even though the agreement was made, a party is, or the merger took place "outside Singapore", if the
-- prohibition is infringed. s 33(4): "Nothing in this Part applies to any activity carried on by, any agreement entered into or
-- any conduct on the part of" (a) the Government; (b) any statutory body; (c) any person acting on behalf of either.
-- s 33(5): "Despite subsection (4)", the Part applies to such statutory body, or person acting on behalf of a statutory body, "as
-- the Minister may, by order in the Gazette, prescribe". There is no such power for the Government.
DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    `a Singapore company`
    `a company outside Singapore`
    `the Government`
    `a statutory body`
    `a person acting for a statutory body`
    `a person acting for the Government`

GIVEN `the actor` IS AN Actor, `the Minister has prescribed it by order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Part 3 applies to` IF
    CONSIDER `the actor`
    WHEN `the Government` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a person acting for the Government` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a statutory body` THEN `the Minister has prescribed it by order`
    WHEN `a person acting for a statutory body` THEN `the Minister has prescribed it by order`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `34, 35 and Third Schedule -- anti-competitive agreements`

-- s 34(1): agreements between undertakings, decisions by associations of undertakings or concerted practices "which have as their
-- object or effect the prevention, restriction or distortion of competition within Singapore are prohibited", subject to s 35.
-- (2) examples: price fixing, limiting production, sharing markets, discrimination, tying. (3) the offending provision is "void".
-- s 35: the prohibition "does not apply to such matter as may be specified in the Third Schedule". Third Schedule exclusions that
-- reach s 34: para 1 services of general economic interest (insofar as the prohibition "would obstruct" their tasks); para 2 to
-- comply with "any requirement imposed by or under any written law"; paras 3 and 4 Ministerial orders (international obligations;
-- "exceptional and compelling reasons of public policy"); para 5 another regulator's competition jurisdiction; para 6 specified
-- activities (letters, piped water, wastewater, buses, rail, cargo terminals); para 7 the Automated Clearing House; para 8 "any
-- vertical agreement, other than such vertical agreement as the Minister may by order specify"; para 9 net economic benefit;
-- para 10 directly related and necessary to a merger; para 11(1) agreements that result in a merger.
-- Para 9: the agreement "contributes to (a) improving production or distribution; or (b) promoting technical or economic progress,
-- but which does not (c) impose ... restrictions which are not indispensable ... or (d) afford ... the possibility of eliminating
-- competition in respect of a substantial part of the goods or services".
DECLARE Agreement HAS
    `has an anti-competitive object or effect in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `would obstruct a service of general economic interest` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is made to comply with a legal requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is excluded by a Ministerial order` IS A BOOLEAN
    `falls under another regulator's competition law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `relates to a specified activity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `relates to the Automated Clearing House` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a vertical agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a vertical agreement specified by Ministerial order` IS A BOOLEAN
    `improves production or distribution or promotes progress` IS A BOOLEAN
    `imposes restrictions that are not indispensable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `could eliminate competition in a substantial part` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is directly related and necessary to a merger` IS A BOOLEAN
    `results in a merger` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the agreement` IS AN Agreement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agreement has net economic benefit` IF
        `the agreement`'s `improves production or distribution or promotes progress`
    AND (NOT `the agreement`'s `imposes restrictions that are not indispensable`)
    AND (NOT `the agreement`'s `could eliminate competition in a substantial part`)

GIVEN `the agreement` IS AN Agreement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agreement is excluded from section 34` IF
        `the agreement`'s `would obstruct a service of general economic interest`
    OR  `the agreement`'s `is made to comply with a legal requirement`
    OR  `the agreement`'s `is excluded by a Ministerial order`
    OR  `the agreement`'s `falls under another regulator's competition law`
    OR  `the agreement`'s `relates to a specified activity`
    OR  `the agreement`'s `relates to the Automated Clearing House`
    OR  (`the agreement`'s `is a vertical agreement` AND (NOT `the agreement`'s `is a vertical agreement specified by Ministerial order`))
    OR  `the agreement has net economic benefit` `the agreement`
    OR  `the agreement`'s `is directly related and necessary to a merger`
    OR  `the agreement`'s `results in a merger`

GIVEN `the agreement` IS AN Agreement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agreement infringes section 34` IF
        `the agreement`'s `has an anti-competitive object or effect in Singapore`
    AND (NOT `the agreement is excluded from section 34` `the agreement`)

§§ `47, 48 and Third Schedule -- abuse of a dominant position`

-- s 47(1): "any conduct on the part of one or more undertakings which amounts to the abuse of a dominant position in any market in
-- Singapore is prohibited". (2) examples: predatory behaviour, limiting production to the prejudice of consumers, discrimination,
-- tying. (3) "'dominant position' means a dominant position within Singapore or elsewhere".
-- s 48: the Third Schedule applies. Of its exclusions, paras 1, 2(2), 3(4), 4(4), 5, 6, 7, 10 and 11(2) reach s 47. Paras 8
-- (vertical agreements) and 9 (net economic benefit) are expressed to apply to "the section 34 prohibition" only.
DECLARE Conduct HAS
    `the undertaking is dominant in Singapore or elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN
    `amounts to an abuse in a market in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `obstructs a service of general economic interest` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is engaged in to comply with a legal requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is disapplied by a Ministerial order` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is under another regulator's competition law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `concerns a specified activity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `concerns the Automated Clearing House` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is directly related and necessary to implementing a merger` IS A BOOLEAN
    `itself results in a merger` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is excluded from section 47` IF
        `the conduct`'s `obstructs a service of general economic interest`
    OR  `the conduct`'s `is engaged in to comply with a legal requirement`
    OR  `the conduct`'s `is disapplied by a Ministerial order`
    OR  `the conduct`'s `is under another regulator's competition law`
    OR  `the conduct`'s `concerns a specified activity`
    OR  `the conduct`'s `concerns the Automated Clearing House`
    OR  `the conduct`'s `is directly related and necessary to implementing a merger`
    OR  `the conduct`'s `itself results in a merger`

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct infringes section 47` IF
        `the conduct`'s `the undertaking is dominant in Singapore or elsewhere`
    AND `the conduct`'s `amounts to an abuse in a market in Singapore`
    AND (NOT `the conduct is excluded from section 47` `the conduct`)

§§ `54, 55 and Fourth Schedule -- mergers`

-- s 54(1): "mergers that have resulted, or may be expected to result, in a substantial lessening of competition within any market
-- in Singapore for goods or services are prohibited". (2) a merger occurs if undertakings merge, control is acquired, or assets are
-- acquired so as to replace the seller's business. (7) "a merger is not to be deemed to occur if" (a) the acquirer is "a receiver
-- or liquidator acting as such or is an underwriter acting as such"; (b) all undertakings are under the control of the same
-- undertaking; (c) control is acquired "solely as a result of a testamentary disposition, intestacy or the right of survivorship
-- under a joint tenancy"; (d) a securities dealer holds securities "on a temporary basis" and votes only to arrange disposal
-- "within the specified period" and not to determine the target's competitive activities (subss (8), (9)). (10) "specified period"
-- is 12 months from acquiring control, or a longer period the Commission determines where disposal within 12 months is not
-- reasonably possible.
-- INFERENCE: subs (9) speaks of the PURPOSE of voting (disposal "within the specified period"). It is modelled here as the dealer
-- having held control for no longer than 12 months or any longer period the Commission set (0 where none was set).
-- s 55 and Fourth Schedule: para 1 a merger (a) approved by a Minister or regulator other than the Commission under a written-law
-- approval requirement "(other than section 19 of the Significant Investments Review Act 2024)" [S 18/2026]; (b) approved by the
-- Monetary Authority of Singapore; (c) under another regulator's competition law; para 2 involving a specified-activity undertaking;
-- para 3 "if the economic efficiencies arising or that may arise from the merger outweigh the adverse effects".
DECLARE Merger HAS
    `is a merger under section 54(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `acquirer is a receiver, liquidator or underwriter acting as such` IS A BOOLEAN
    `all parties are under common control` IS A BOOLEAN
    `control passed solely by will, intestacy or survivorship` IS A BOOLEAN
    `acquirer is a securities dealer holding temporarily` IS A BOOLEAN
    `dealer votes only to arrange disposal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months the dealer has held control` IS A NUMBER
    `longer period in months set by the Commission` IS A NUMBER
    `substantially lessens competition in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `approved by a Minister or regulator under written law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that approval was under section 19 of the Significant Investments Review Act 2024` IS A BOOLEAN
    `approved by the Monetary Authority of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `within another regulator's competition jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `involves a specified-activity undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
    `efficiencies outweigh the adverse effects` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the larger of` MEANS IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` MEANS IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `the merger` IS A Merger
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the dealer exception applies` IF
        `the merger`'s `acquirer is a securities dealer holding temporarily`
    AND `the merger`'s `dealer votes only to arrange disposal`
    AND `the merger`'s `months the dealer has held control` AT MOST
            `the larger of` 12 (`the merger`'s `longer period in months set by the Commission`)

GIVEN `the merger` IS A Merger
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a merger occurs` IF
        `the merger`'s `is a merger under section 54(2)`
    AND (NOT `the merger`'s `acquirer is a receiver, liquidator or underwriter acting as such`)
    AND (NOT `the merger`'s `all parties are under common control`)
    AND (NOT `the merger`'s `control passed solely by will, intestacy or survivorship`)
    AND (NOT `the dealer exception applies` `the merger`)

GIVEN `the merger` IS A Merger
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the merger is excluded by the Fourth Schedule` IF
        (`the merger`'s `approved by a Minister or regulator under written law`
            AND (NOT `the merger`'s `that approval was under section 19 of the Significant Investments Review Act 2024`))
    OR  `the merger`'s `approved by the Monetary Authority of Singapore`
    OR  `the merger`'s `within another regulator's competition jurisdiction`
    OR  `the merger`'s `involves a specified-activity undertaking`
    OR  `the merger`'s `efficiencies outweigh the adverse effects`

GIVEN `the merger` IS A Merger
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the merger infringes section 54` IF
        `a merger occurs` `the merger`
    AND `the merger`'s `substantially lessens competition in Singapore`
    AND (NOT `the merger is excluded by the Fourth Schedule` `the merger`)

§§ `69(3), (4) -- the ceiling on a financial penalty`

-- s 69(3): the Commission "may impose a financial penalty only if it is satisfied that the infringement has been committed
-- intentionally or negligently". (4): "No financial penalty ... may exceed 10% or such other percentage of such turnover of the
-- business of the undertaking in Singapore for each year of infringement for such period, up to a maximum of 3 years, as the
-- Minister may, by order in the Gazette, prescribe."
-- INFERENCE: the subsection is read here as 10% of Singapore turnover per year of infringement, counting at most 3 years, with a
-- constant annual turnover. Whether a Ministerial order prescribes another percentage or a turnover measure was not checked.
GIVEN `annual Singapore turnover` IS A NUMBER, `years of infringement` IS A NUMBER, `intentional or negligent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum financial penalty` MEANS
    IF `intentional or negligent`
    THEN `annual Singapore turnover` TIMES 10 DIVIDED BY 100 TIMES (`the smaller of` `years of infringement` 3)
    ELSE 0

§§ `71(3) -- appeals do not suspend`

-- s 71(3): "Except in the case of an appeal against the imposition, or the amount, of a financial penalty, the making of an appeal
-- under this section does not suspend the effect of the decision to which the appeal relates."
GIVEN `the appeal is against a financial penalty or its amount` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appeal suspends the decision` IF `the appeal is against a financial penalty or its amount`

§§ `75, 77, 83 -- offences around investigations`

-- s 75(1): failing to comply with a requirement imposed under s 61A, 63, 64 or 65 is an offence. (2) for a requirement to produce
-- a document, it is a defence "to prove that (a) the document was not in the person's possession or under the person's control;
-- and (b) it was not reasonably practicable for the person to comply". (3) for a requirement to provide information, answer a
-- question, explain a document or say where one is, a defence to prove "a reasonable excuse". (4) failing to comply with a
-- requirement under s 61A, 63 or 64 "shall not be an offence if the person imposing the requirement has failed to act in accordance
-- with that section" -- s 65 (entry under warrant) is not in that list.
-- s 83: where no penalty is expressly provided, "a fine not exceeding $10,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months
-- or ... both". No penalty is expressly provided in ss 75-78 as deposited.
DECLARE Requirement IS ONE OF
    `a section 61A notice`
    `a section 63 investigation requirement`
    `a section 64 entry without warrant`
    `a section 65 entry under warrant`

DECLARE Demand IS ONE OF
    `to produce a document`
    `to give information or answer a question`

GIVEN `the requirement` IS A Requirement, `the demand` IS A Demand, `failed to comply` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the imposer acted in accordance with the section` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved no possession and not reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the failure to comply is an offence` IF
        `failed to comply`
    AND (    `the imposer acted in accordance with the section`
         OR  `the requirement` EQUALS `a section 65 entry under warrant`)
    AND (CONSIDER `the demand`
         WHEN `to produce a document` THEN NOT `proved no possession and not reasonably practicable`
         OTHERWISE NOT `proved a reasonable excuse`)

-- s 77(1): providing information to the Commission or its officers is an offence if "(a) the information is false or misleading in
-- a material particular; and (b) he or she knows that it is false or misleading in a material particular or is reckless as to
-- whether it is".
GIVEN `false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN, `knew it` IS A BOOLEAN, `was reckless` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `giving the information is an offence` IF
    `false or misleading in a material particular` AND (`knew it` OR `was reckless`)

`the general maximum fine` MEANS 10000
`the general maximum months of imprisonment` MEANS 12

§§ `86 -- private action`

-- s 86(1): "Any person who suffers loss or damage directly as a result of an infringement" of s 34, 47 or 54 has a right of action
-- against an undertaking party to it. (2) no action "until after a decision ... has established" the infringement (a Commission
-- decision under s 68 or a decision on appeal), and not during the appeal periods in (4) -- which include any pending appeal (5).
-- (6) "No action ... may be brought after the end of 2 years after the relevant period specified in subsection (4)." (7) the court
-- accepts the decision as "final and conclusive". (9) "Nothing in this section confers on any party to an agreement which
-- infringes the section 34 prohibition a right of action for relief."
-- The 2 years are modelled as 24 months; an action at exactly 24 months is treated as in time (INFERENCE on "after the end of").
GIVEN `suffered loss directly from the infringement` IS A BOOLEAN, `a decision has established the infringement` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the appeal periods have run out` IS A BOOLEAN, `months since the appeal periods ended` IS A NUMBER,
      `the claimant is a party to the infringing section 34 agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a private action may be brought` IF
        `suffered loss directly from the infringement`
    AND `a decision has established the infringement`
    AND `the appeal periods have run out`
    AND `months since the appeal periods ended` AT MOST 24
    AND (NOT `the claimant is a party to the infringing section 34 agreement`)
